 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532698,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose you want to a build a container to hold 2 cubic feet of fabric swatches. You want to cover the container in laminate costing $10 per square foot. What are the dimensions of the container that is the most economical? What is the cost?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>If all six sides are the same, then the ideal volume is <span data-math=\"V = {s^3}\"></span>. \n</p><table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2{\\text{ f}}{{\\text{t}}^3} = {s^3}\"></span></td>\n<td>Find the cube root of both sides.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"1.26{\\text{ ft }} = s\"></span></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\nFind the surface area.<p></p>\n<p>The rectangular base has an area <span data-math=\"{\\text{B  =  LW  =  (1}}{\\text{.26 ft)(1}}{\\text{.26 ft)  =  1}}{\\text{.59 f}}{{\\text{t}}^{\\text{2}}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The perimeter of the base <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  }}p{\\text{  =  2(1}}{\\text{.26 ft)  +  2(1 }}{\\text{.26 ft)  =  5}}{\\text{.04 ft}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area <span data-math=\" = {\\text{ }}2B + ph = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {1.59{\\text{ f}}{{\\text{t}}^2}} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}\\left( {5.04{\\text{ ft}}} \\right)\\left( {1.26{\\text{ ft}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}9.5304{\\text{ f}}{{\\text{t}}^2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Make a conversion factor out of the cost of laminate.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"9.5304{\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{sq ft}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\$ 10}}{{1{\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{sq ft}}}}}}} \\right) \\approx \\$ 95.30\"></span></p>\n<p>The ideal dimensions are 1.26 feet wide by 1.26 feet long by 1.26 feet high at a cost of $95.30.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"1.26\\,{\\text{ft}}\\,{\\text{wide}}\\, \\times \\,1.26\\,{\\text{ft}}\\,{\\text{long}}\\, \\times \\,1.26\\,{\\text{ft}}\\,{\\text{high}},\">1.26\\,{\\text{ft}}\\,{\\text{wide}}\\, \\times \\,1.26\\,{\\text{ft}}\\,{\\text{long}}\\, \\times \\,1.26\\,{\\text{ft}}\\,{\\text{high}},</span> $95.26"
    }
   ],
